{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_2zwNPDEzya6CttfrK9CFdN9e","content":"1\t# tri-planner\n2\t\n3\tGenerates structured triathlon workouts and pushes them to Intervals.icu, which\n4\texports them to the athlete's Garmin watch through Garmin Connect.\n5\t\n6\t- `gen.py` turns a plan (`plans/*.json`) into the body for\n7\t  `POST /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events` (an event with `workout_doc`).\n8\t- `push.sh` posts it (needs `INTERVALS_API_KEY` and `ATHLETE_ID`).\n9\t- `readback/` holds what the API returned for the last pushed event and\n10\t  notes on what the watch displayed.\n11\t\n12\tAthlete thresholds live in Intervals (LTHR 172 for this athlete). HR targets\n13\tin plans are percentages of LTHR; Intervals converts them to bpm at export.\n14\t\n15\t```\n16\tpython3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json\n17\t./push.sh event.json\n18\t```"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_1LKPBny0Lso4aM9wcmDxlXIe","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"Build an Intervals.icu event body (workout_doc) from a plan file.\n3\t\n4\tUsage: python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json\n5\t\"\"\"\n6\timport json\n7\timport sys\n8\t\n9\t\n10\tdef hr_target(step):\n11\t    \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\"\"\"\n12\t    lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n13\t    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}\n14\t\n15\t\n16\tdef build_step(step):\n17\t    out = {\"duration\": step[\"minutes\"] * 60}\n18\t    if \"hr_pct\" in step:\n19\t        out[\"hr\"] = hr_target(step)\n20\t    if \"label\" in step:\n21\t        out[\"text\"] = step[\"label\"]\n22\t    return out\n23\t\n24\t\n25\tdef build_doc(plan):\n26\t    steps = []\n27\t    for block in plan[\"steps\"]:\n28\t        if \"repeat\" in block:\n29\t            steps.append({\n30\t                \"reps\": block[\"repeat\"],\n31\t                \"steps\": [build_step(s) for s in block[\"steps\"]],\n32\t            })\n33\t        else:\n34\t            steps.append(build_step(block))\n35\t    return {\"steps\": steps}\n36\t\n37\t\n38\tdef build_event(plan):\n39\t    return {\n40\t        \"category\": \"WORKOUT\",\n41\t        \"type\": plan[\"sport\"],\n42\t        \"name\": plan[\"name\"],\n43\t        \"start_date_local\": plan[\"date\"] + \"T00:00:00\",\n44\t        \"workout_doc\": build_doc(plan),\n45\t    }\n46\t\n47\t\n48\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n49\t    with open(sys.argv[1]) as f:\n50\t        plan = json.load(f)\n51\t    json.dump(build_event(plan), sys.stdout, indent=2)\n52\t    print()"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_JLZ10w7rDK57EUPJQdqf7mL2","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"name\": \"Tempo run 45\",\n3\t  \"sport\": \"Run\",\n4\t  \"date\": \"2026-10-20\",\n5\t  \"steps\": [\n6\t    {\"label\": \"Warm-up easy\", \"minutes\": 10, \"hr_pct\": [68, 75]},\n7\t    {\"repeat\": 3, \"steps\": [\n8\t      {\"label\": \"Tempo\", \"minutes\": 8, \"hr_pct\": [88, 93]},\n9\t      {\"label\": \"Float\", \"minutes\": 2, \"hr_pct\": [75, 82]}\n10\t    ]},\n11\t    {\"label\": \"Cool-down\", \"minutes\": 5, \"hr_pct\": [65, 72]}\n12\t  ]\n13\t}"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_LtIKFY3Fu2OXSzqHiKcsfJzP","content":"1\t# What the watch showed for event 184233 (Tempo run 45)\n2\t\n3\tIntervals: LTHR 172. Watch (Forerunner 965): auto-detected LTHR 168, zones\n4\tZ1 <118, Z2 118–137, Z3 137–151, Z4 151–162, Z5 >162.\n5\t\n6\t`GET /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events/184233` returned the event exactly as we sent\n7\tit (see `event-184233-as-sent.json`); `workout_doc.steps` is populated, so the\n8\tAPI accepted it.\n9\t\n10\t| step | planned (% LTHR) | expected on watch (× 172) | watch displayed |\n11\t|---|---|---|---|\n12\t| Warm-up easy | 68–75 | 117–129 | 118–137 |\n13\t| Tempo | 88–93 | 151–160 | 151–162 |\n14\t| Float | 75–82 | 129–141 | 137–151 |\n15\t| Cool-down | 65–72 | 112–124 | 118–137 |\n16\t\n17\tEvery corridor shows up as one of the watch's own zone bands, not the range we\n18\tplanned. Changing the watch's LTHR to 172 moves the bands but they are still\n19\tzone edges, never 151–160 or 129–141. Earlier tries: `units: \"bpm\"` with\n20\tabsolute values made the watch show 214–249 bpm; `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` made\n21\tevery target a constant 101."}
